# Layer 2 (CR 613.1b) with ADR-0037's zone correction. Control Magic's
# S:Mode$ Continuous | AffectedDefined$ Enchanted | GainControl$ You makes the
# human the controller of the AI's Grizzly Bears. The first state-based-action
# pass of StartTurn applies it and moves the Bears to the human's battlefield
# (GameAction.controllerChangeZoneCorrection): the human controls them, the AI
# still owns them (Owner:ai), and they are summoning sick under their new
# controller. Without the layer they would stay on the AI's side.
# It is the AI's turn on purpose: Java applies a preexisting steal at load,
# before any untap step, while this port applies it at the first pass after
# the untap step, so only the non-active controller gives the same result in
# both (an active thief's untap step would clear the sickness in Java).
startturn ai
